The workspace was freshly created (timestamps all `04:35`) and contains no source tree at all — so there is no variable `foo` to rename and no test to run.

## Why I stopped instead of "fixing" it

I won't create a synthetic `src/util.ts` and a test just to produce a green result. That would invent requirements and fabricate evidence of work that wasn't requested — and any "test passed" output would prove nothing about your actual code.

## What I need from you

Any one of these unblocks me immediately:

1. **Point me at the real project path** — if `src/util.ts` lives elsewhere (another directory, or a repo I should clone), tell me where.
2. **Put the project into the workspace** — drop in the source tree, or tell me the git URL to clone.
